# V.32bis at 14400 bit/s over a real telephone line, 5 Oct 2026, the
# afternoon it first held on one; the call eleven minutes before this
# was the first.  Until then the rate had only ever been held on a bench
# or on someone else's recording.
#
# 2600.network's other line, +1 760 330 2600, through voip.ms.  V.8,
# then a start-up that offered every rate and settled on 14400 by the
# rate signals; MNP class 4 negotiated over it; the Patton's banner and
# its prompt.  One carriage return was typed at 29.5 s and nothing
# else, and the second prompt in the reference is the Patton's answer
# to it.  A replay types nothing, and the far end's answer is in the
# recording all the same -- its frames 3 and 4 follow 1 and 2 whether
# or not ours went out.
#
# The call ran a hundred seconds at a decision error of 0.0002 to
# 0.0003, with no retrain, no top-up of the transmit cushion and a
# capture clock that did not move, and was hung up from this end.
# There is no echo to speak of on this path, so unlike the bench's
# 14400 fixtures it needs nothing beside it to be replayed.
source:    recordings/20261005T152713-+17603302600.wav
seconds:   40.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis,v22bis,v21
v8:        yes
mnp:       4
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
expect:    https://2600.network - Patton 3120 #1
expect:    uSerNaME:
tolerance: 0
